& [DictatedHypothesis]
  + conventional development estimates may fit a model whose jobs are not semantically primed
  + SOP supplies inference-priming operators that direct inference toward intended purposes
  + the new SOP articulation layer should strengthen that effect
  + optimizing SOP for inference may complete inference-dominated work another two to three times faster

& [SelectedElements]
  + SOPArticulationCompiler transforms one governed SOP into a bounded model-facing execution articulation without changing its authority or requirements
  + PrimingOperator is one source-bound projection instruction that reduces rediscovery of a subject distinction coordinate transform evidence gate fault or completion condition
  + ArticulationProfile binds model provider task class context ceiling tool policy compiler version and projection strategy for one experiment
  + PrimingReceipt binds selected omitted and invalidated operators projected bytes token estimate scope and governing source identities
  + TaskThroughputModel separates inference-sensitive work from fixed external execution and verification costs

& [PerformanceMeaning]
  + inference acceleration means lower time to an accepted task result through fewer reasoning tokens model calls repeated reads retrieval detours tool mistakes branch repairs unsupported assumptions and context reconstruction passes
  + it does not initially mean higher raw model tokens per second lower neural compute per token a wider hardware context window or changed model weights
  + prefix reuse provider prompt caching or K/V reuse may later be measured separately and cannot be inferred from semantic priming alone
  + a two-to-three-times gain is an empirical target for inference-dominated tasks and not a current measurement or universal multiplier

& [CompilerPassDirection]
  + GoverningAnchorClosure selects applicable requirements constraints denials authority boundaries and invalidators
  + SemanticCoordinateBinding selects exact subject distinctions relations file symbol graph and lifecycle coordinates needed for the next operations
  + TrajectoryArticulation projects intended transforms dependency order branch conditions and completion cues
  + EvidenceLookahead projects expected receipts acceptance gates proof obligations and partial-output refusals before action
  + FaultLookahead projects known operational faults ambiguous boundaries and forbidden shortcuts
  + CommonScopeFactoring emits one stable covenant shared across all turns and jobs while retaining additive job-local stitches
  + ResearchFrontierArticulation projects material unknowns active prospects methods and stop rules when research is justified
  + MinimumBasisReduction removes only operators whose absence passes restoration and frame-equivalence checks

& [SafetyAgainstOverpriming]
  + every operator binds sources applicability scope intended transform completion invalidation and nonauthority
  + compiler output retains counterevidence ambiguity alternative branches and explicit unknowns needed to avoid premature convergence
  + unsupported convenient terms familiar vocabulary and prior successful paths cannot displace mandatory governing anchors
  + an invalidated source changed task changed model profile conflicting receipt or drifted frame forces recompilation or refusal
  + priming quality is rejected when speed improves by reducing requirement coverage evidence quality semantic correctness safety or authority correspondence

& [EstimateModel]
  + BaselineWork is the conventional unprimed estimate for the same accepted outcome
  + CurrentSOPFactor measures observed improvement from ordinary governed SOP source navigation reentry and evidence cues
  + CompiledArticulationFactor measures additional improvement from deliberate operator selection projection and minimization
  + FixedWork includes Rust compilation tests downloads hardware provider process network publication external approvals and other costs not shortened by model semantic priming
  + one candidate estimate is TotalTime equals FixedWork plus InferenceSensitiveWork divided by CurrentSOPFactor times CompiledArticulationFactor
  + do not divide FixedWork or blocked waiting time by an inference factor
  + recalibrate factors by task class because source formation code implementation debugging research integration and physical deployment have different inference fractions

& [WholeProjectBoundary]
  + if most of a bounded provider-free design task is inference-sensitive a two-to-three-times articulation gain may approach the observed wall-time gain
  + if only sixty to eighty percent of a product slice is inference-sensitive fixed work limits the total gain even when that portion becomes two-to-three-times faster
  + at seventy percent inference-sensitive work and a two-and-one-half-times articulation factor the maximum whole-slice gain is about one-and-seven-tenths times before other overhead changes
  + project estimates should therefore publish inference fraction fixed fraction measured factors uncertainty and blocker assumptions rather than one global multiplier

& [ExperimentArms]
  + Arm0 receives the same task with only minimal governing authority and no optional priming packet
  + Arm1 receives the current human-authored SOP and ordinary reentry material
  + Arm2 receives compiled lookahead stitches and the deterministic StitchSelector output
  + Arm3 receives Arm2 plus MinimumRecoverableFrame scope-wide covenant and restoration-tested reduction
  + Arm4 may add the ResearchOpportunitySurface only for tasks whose ResearchNeedDisposition admits research
  + every arm retains identical source state model provider sampling tools authority budgets execution environment and acceptance gates

& [Measurements]
  + measure time to first correct operation time to accepted closure input output and total tokens provider calls tool calls file reads redundant reads corrections plan repairs gate failures and unsupported assumptions
  + measure final requirement coverage evidence completeness fault count safety correspondence and reviewer disposition as non-regression outcomes
  + measure compiler time projected context cost restoration checks and recompilation count so priming overhead is included
  + retain task model provider profile compiler profile and exact operator identities for every trial
  + report median tail distribution and refusal causes rather than selecting the fastest successful example

& [CalibrationAndEstimation]
  + recent Cantor work suggests governed source reentry and existing substrates can outperform conventional sequential estimates but the observation is not a controlled priming experiment
  + first calibrate provider-free fixture tasks where exact outputs and acceptance are deterministic
  + then perform live A/B only under exact pinned provider and model availability with zero synthetic substitution
  + update future estimates from accepted measured task-class factors and preserve the older estimate assumptions for audit
  + lower estimates only for work surfaces whose measurements support the corresponding factor

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes exact source custody and later SJS processing only
  + no canonical compiler schema operator vocabulary prompt projection score weight speedup estimate reduction satisfaction signature Rust implementation provider call model result live experiment autonomous execution workspace mutation remote host FPGA Minecraft physical effect or performance claim is authorized
